(ned SET PROBE HEIGHT -- step 2 of the probing reset, after FIND SHOULDER.)
(Operator 2026-08-11: "have another button below that is SET PROBE height,)
(user goes to height and just clicks".)

(WHAT PB ENDS UP HOLDING, in the operator's own list:)
(  a  XY of the probe          #5181 #5182   written by the G30.1 below)
(  b  the G30 height           #5183         written by the G30.1 below)
(  c  nose height              #3010         FIND SHOULDER writes it)
(  d  plunge from G30, taken all the way to the Z limit plus 1 mm)
(                              #3007         RECOMPUTED HERE)

(d IS A FUNCTION OF b, WHICH IS WHY IT IS RECOMPUTED IN THE SAME CLICK.)
(Move the probe height by hand and leave the old plunge behind and the two)
(are out of step by exactly however far the height moved. That is the same)
(class of stale-derived-value bug that had the shoulder driving 157 mm past)
(the Z soft limit, and it is not worth repeating.)

(G30.1 records the CURRENT position in MACHINE coordinates. That is the)
(reason the shoulder step uses it too: no work-to-machine conversion to get)
(wrong, which is precisely what broke the shoulder plunge.)

(NO MOTION. The button only reads where the machine already is. Whatever the)
(operator jogged to IS the answer, so moving first could only make the)
(recorded number describe somewhere they did not choose.)

(ANY TOOL MAY BE IN THE SPINDLE. Operator 2026-08-11: "the whole point is)
(this calibration is done with an arbitrary tool". Nothing here measures the)
(tool -- it records a height the operator picked and the travel left below)
(it, and both are true whatever is in the taper. The NOSE height is step 1's)
(job and that one does need an empty spindle.)
o<cal_probe_height> sub
  #<zmin> = #1        (Z soft limit, machine, passed by the caller)
  o1 if [#<zmin> EQ 0]
    (abort, SET PROBE HEIGHT: no Z soft limit passed - refusing to guess the plunge)
  o1 endif
  o5 if [#<_metric> EQ 0]
    (abort, SET PROBE HEIGHT: switch to MM first)
  o5 endif
  G30.1
  (MACHINE MINUS MACHINE: #5183 was just written by G30.1 and is the start)
  (height in machine terms, zmin is the machine soft limit. Stop 1 mm short.)
  #<plunge> = [#5183 - [#<zmin> + 1.0]]
  o4 if [#<plunge> LE 0]
    (abort, SET PROBE HEIGHT: this height is already at the Z soft limit - no room to probe)
  o4 endif
  #3007 = #<plunge>
  #3077 = #<plunge>
  (PRINT, SET PROBE HEIGHT: G30 recorded at X #5181 Y #5182 Z #5183 machine - PB starts every tool probe from here.)
  (PRINT, SET PROBE HEIGHT: plunge #3007 mm - from that height down to 1 mm above the #<zmin> soft limit.)
  (DEBUG, PROBE HEIGHT SET: Z #5183 plunge #3007)
o<cal_probe_height> endsub
M2 (end program)
